STABLE
------

0.2.0
-----
== Backwards-incompatible: requires cat_tools 0.3.0 or later
Any older cat_tools is rejected at `CREATE EXTENSION` and `ALTER EXTENSION
UPDATE`. Previously any cat_tools version was accepted.

== Backwards-incompatible: `reg*` columns removed from `_object_reference._object_oid`
The `regclass`, `regconfig`, `regdictionary`, `regnamespace`, `regoperator`,
`regprocedure` and `regtype` columns are gone, replaced by plain `oid`
`classid` and `objid` columns. Anything that reads those internal columns
directly breaks. The `count_nulls` extension is no longer required.

== Special update step
Run `ALTER EXTENSION cat_tools UPDATE` to 0.3.0 or later before `ALTER
EXTENSION object_reference UPDATE`.

== Add `object__describe()`, `object__identity()` and `object__cleanup()`
`object__describe()` and `object__identity()` wrap `pg_describe_object()` and
`pg_identify_object()`. `object__cleanup()` deletes an object's reference
if nothing else still uses it, ignoring `foreign_key_violation`. It now runs
automatically when an object is removed from its last object group.

== Refuse to track temporary objects
`object__getsert()` raises an error for objects in a `pg_temp*` or
`pg_toast_temp*` schema.

== Refuse to track object_reference's own objects
`object__getsert()` raises `feature_not_supported` for any member of the
object_reference extension itself.

== Partitioned tables and indexes are unsupported object types
They are listed by `object_reference.unsupported()`, because
`pg_get_object_address()` can't round-trip them.

== Stop overriding `client_min_messages` during install
`CREATE EXTENSION` already raises it as needed; the script's own setting
could lower a stricter caller's level.
